<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Functional Gradient</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023b</a></cite> present the chain rule for functional gradients, which is detailed in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ A.2 Functional Gradient ‣ Appendix A Additional Discussions ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gelfand and Silverman, 2000</a>)</cite>, and utilize the Fréchet derivative to calculate the derivative of the evaluation functional in RKHS, as shown in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Lemma 6. ‣ A.2 Functional Gradient ‣ Appendix A Additional Discussions ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Coleman, 2012</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Chain rule for functional gradients)

For differentiable functions <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(F):\mathbb{R}\mapsto\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(F):\mathbb{R}\mapsto\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that depend on functionals <math id="Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(f):\mathcal{H}\mapsto\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(f):\mathcal{H}\mapsto\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the chain rule is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{f}G(F(f))=\frac{\partial G(F(f))}{\partial F(f)}\cdot\nabla_{f}F(f)~." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.052em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{f}G(F(f))=\frac{\partial G(F(f))}{\partial F(f)}\cdot\nabla_{f}F(f)~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The gradient of the evaluation functional at the feature <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left.E_{\bm{x}}(f)=f(\bm{x}):\mathcal{H}\to\mathbb{R}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.E_{\bm{x}}(f)=f(\bm{x}):\mathcal{H}\to\mathbb{R}\right.</annotation></semantics></math>, is given by <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{f}E_{\bm{x}}(f)=K(\bm{x},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>f</mi></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{f}E_{\bm{x}}(f)=K(\bm{x},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(\bm{x},\bm{x}^{\prime}):\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(\bm{x},\bm{x}^{\prime}):\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> represents a feature-based kernel.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>The Derivation of Importance-adaptive Updates in the Parameter Space.</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before providing the detailed derivation, we begin by showing visualizations of general single-head attention learners. Figure <a href="#A1.F2.sf1" title="In Figure 2 ‣ A.3 The Derivation of Importance-adaptive Updates in the Parameter Space. ‣ Appendix A Additional Discussions ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a> depicts a multi-output self-attention learner, Figure <a href="#A1.F2.sf2" title="In Figure 2 ‣ A.3 The Derivation of Importance-adaptive Updates in the Parameter Space. ‣ Appendix A Additional Discussions ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a> presents a multi-output masked self-attention learner, and Figure <a href="#A1.F2.sf3" title="In Figure 2 ‣ A.3 The Derivation of Importance-adaptive Updates in the Parameter Space. ‣ Appendix A Additional Discussions ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(c)</span></a> illustrates a multi-output cross-attention learner. The formulations for the masked self-attention and cross-attention learners are presented in Equation <a href="#A1.Ex1" title="In A.3 The Derivation of Importance-adaptive Updates in the Parameter Space. ‣ Appendix A Additional Discussions ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Masked Self-Attention:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\theta}(\bm{S})=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathcal{Q}(\bm{S})\mathcal{K}(\bm{S})^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}+\bm{M}\right)\mathcal{V}(\bm{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\theta}(\bm{S})=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathcal{Q}(\bm{S})\mathcal{K}(\bm{S})^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}+\bm{M}\right)\mathcal{V}(\bm{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E23.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Cross-Attention:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\theta}(\bm{S},\bm{S}^{\prime})=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathcal{Q}(\bm{S})\mathcal{K}(\bm{S}^{\prime})^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)\mathcal{V}(\bm{S}^{\prime})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\theta}(\bm{S},\bm{S}^{\prime})=\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathcal{Q}(\bm{S})\mathcal{K}(\bm{S}^{\prime})^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)\mathcal{V}(\bm{S}^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}\in\mathbb{R}^{S\times S}</annotation></semantics></math> is a is a strictly upper triangular matrix, with zeros on and below the diagonal and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> in every element above the diagonal.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20461v1/self_attention_m.svg" id="A1.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:181/165;" width="181" height="165"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20461v1/masked_self_attention_m.svg" id="A1.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:181/164;" width="181" height="164"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20461v1/cross_attention_m.svg" id="A1.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:181/165;" width="181" height="165"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>An illustration of the workflow for different multi-output attention learners, with input sequence <math id="A1.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (in the case of cross-attention).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the derivative of an ANN with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=1</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning that each component of the output <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S})}_{(j,:)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S})}_{(j,:)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{V}},\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{Q}_{(:,1)}},\dots,\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{Q}_{(:,p)}},\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{K}_{(:,1)}},\dots,\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{K}_{(:,p)}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{V}},\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{Q}_{(:,1)}},\dots,\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{Q}_{(:,p)}},\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{K}_{(:,1)}},\dots,\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{K}_{(:,p)}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By applying the chain rule, we can compute the derivative of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(\bm{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(\bm{S})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the weight <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> in the value matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\bm{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\bm{S})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial f_{\theta}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\,\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathcal{Q}(\bm{S})\mathcal{K}(\bm{S})^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)\mathcal{V}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">∂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\,\mathrm{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathcal{Q}(\bm{S})\mathcal{K}(\bm{S})^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)\mathcal{V}(\bm{S})}{\partial\bm{W}^{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
