<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Detailed Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4.2 The Functional Evolution of ANN ‣ 4 AtteNT ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By examining the evolution of an ANN through changes in its parameters and from a high-level perspective within the function space, we obtain.</p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)\right]_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)\right]_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[\left\langle\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i})}{\partial\theta^{t}},\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\cdot)}{\partial\theta^{t}}\right\rangle\right]_{N}+o\left(\frac{\partial\theta^{t}}{\partial t}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[\left\langle\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i})}{\partial\theta^{t}},\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\cdot)}{\partial\theta^{t}}\right\rangle\right]_{N}+o\left(\frac{\partial\theta^{t}}{\partial t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Upon reorganizing, we derive</p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)-K_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i},\cdot)\right]_{N}=o\left(\frac{\partial\theta^{t}}{\partial t}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)-K_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i},\cdot)\right]_{N}=o\left(\frac{\partial\theta^{t}}{\partial t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By integrating the parameter evolution</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\theta^{t}}{\partial t}=-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\theta^{t}}=-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i})}{\partial\theta^{t}}\right]_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\theta^{t}}{\partial t}=-\eta\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\theta^{t}}=-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i})}{\partial\theta^{t}}\right]_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">into the remainder, we get</p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)-K_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i},\cdot)\right]_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)-K_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i},\cdot)\right]_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle o\left(-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i})}{\partial\theta^{t}}\right]_{N}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle o\left(-\frac{\eta}{NS}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]\cdot\left[\frac{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i})}{\partial\theta^{t}}\right]_{N}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">When training an ANN with a convex loss <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is convex in terms of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> but not necessarily in terms of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, the following limit holds for the vector: <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]=\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\left[\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1}),\bm{y}_{1})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{1})},\dots,\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}(f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N}),\bm{y}_{N})}{\partial f_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{N})}\right]=\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the right-hand side of this equation is a higher-order infinitesimal relative to the left, maintaining this equality results in the conclusion that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\ \left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)-K_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i},\cdot)\right]_{N}=\bm{0}~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\ \left[K({\bm{S}_{i}},\cdot)-K_{\theta^{t}}(\bm{S}_{i},\cdot)\right]_{N}=\bm{0}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This suggests that for each training point, <em id="A2.SS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e.</em>, input sequence <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}\in\{\bm{S}_{i}\}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}\in\{\bm{S}_{i}\}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, ANTK converges pointwise to the canonical kernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.2 The Functional Evolution of ANN ‣ 4 AtteNT ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Referring to the definition of the Fréchet derivative in Definition <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Definition 2. ‣ 3 Background ‣ Nonparametric Teaching of Attention Learners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the convexity of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial t}\leq\underbrace{\left\langle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{\theta^{t+1}}},\frac{f_{\theta^{t}}}{\partial t}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}}_{\Upsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial t}\leq\underbrace{\left\langle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{\theta^{t+1}}},\frac{f_{\theta^{t}}}{\partial t}\right\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}}_{\Upsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By computing the Fréchet derivative of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{\theta^{t+1}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial f_{\theta^{t+1}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the evolution of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the term on the right-hand side, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Upsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Upsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, can be expressed as</p>
